index 4479b53..53f0e24 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,28 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## WebMCP tools
+
+The site exposes its client-side functionality to AI agents through [WebMCP](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/). Tools are discoverable in Chromium 146+ with `chrome://flags/#enable-webmcp-testing` enabled; other browsers simply ignore them.
+
+**Declarative tools** (HTML forms annotated with `toolname`, always present in the header flyouts):
+
+| Tool | Where | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `search-articles` | `src/components/SearchFlyout.tsx` | Searches titles and summaries, returns matching articles |
+| `save-article-to-reading-list` | `src/components/ReadingListFlyout.tsx` | Saves an article by slug |
+| `remove-article-from-reading-list` | `src/components/ReadingListFlyout.tsx` | Removes a saved article by slug (available while the list is non-empty) |
+
+**Imperative tools** (`document.modelContext.registerTool()` in `src/scripts/webmcp-tools.ts`, loaded by the main layout):
+
+| Tool | Available | What it does |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `list-articles` | every page | Lists articles, optionally filtered by category |
+| `get-reading-list` | every page | Returns the saved articles |
+| `open-article` | every page | Navigates to an article by slug |
+| `get-current-article` | article pages | Metadata, headings, body text and related articles of the open article |
+| `get-article-popularity` | article pages | Live view count and trending status |
+| `jump-to-article-section` | article pages | Scrolls to a section by heading text |
+
+Tools are re-registered on every view-transition navigation and torn down before the swap. When an agent activates one of the form tools, the matching flyout opens so the user can watch the interaction; active forms are highlighted via `:tool-form-active`.
